---
permalink: /faqs.html
title: "FAQs | American Watchmaking Directory"
description: "Answers about the American Watchmaking Directory: who is listed, how to get a brand added or corrected, where the information comes from, and how to use the data."
navActive: "faqs"
heading: "Frequently asked questions"
intro: 'Tap a question to see the answer. Something else? <a href="/contact.html">Ask us</a>.'
groups:
  - title: "Using the directory"
    items:
      - id: what-is-it
        q: "What is the American Watchmaking Directory?"
        a: >-
          A free, volunteer-run directory of watch brands, independent watchmakers, and the suppliers and repairers who support them, based in the United States, plus a few of our Canadian neighbors. Each listing has a profile page with where the company is based, what it makes, and links to its website and Instagram.
      - id: how-to-use
        q: "How do I use the directory?"
        a: >-
          Search the <a href="/directory.html">directory</a> by name, city or state, and narrow it down by product type, country, state or province, and founding era. Filtered views have their own web address, so you can bookmark or share them. You can also browse the <a href="/map/">map</a> or go <a href="/states/">state by state</a>.
      - id: us-only
        q: "Is the directory only for companies based in the United States?"
        a: >-
          Mostly. We list watch businesses based in the United States, and a selection of Canadian brands to cover North America. We don't list companies based elsewhere.
      - id: made-in-america
        q: "Does a company have to make its watches in America to be listed?"
        a: >-
          No. We list watchmaking businesses based in America, wherever their products are made: here, abroad or both. A listing means a company is based here, not that its products are made here. We don't make our own claims about what is or isn't American made; where a brand describes where its products are made, we report what the brand says.
      - id: who-is-listed
        q: "What kinds of companies do you list?"
        a: >-
          Watch brands and independent watchmakers, plus the companies around them: strap makers, component and parts suppliers, tool suppliers, and repair and restoration shops. Use the product filter in the directory to see each group.
      - id: listing-details
        q: "What information do you include for each company?"
        a: >-
          Where it's based, when it was founded (and revived, for historic names), what it makes, a short description, and links to its website, Instagram and contact email, plus the logo when we have one. Badges show if a company has stopped trading, closed for good, or hasn't launched yet. Where a brand says where its products are made, we report that as the brand's claim, not ours.
  - title: "Getting listed and making changes"
    items:
      - id: get-listed
        q: "How do I get my company listed?"
        a: >-
          Fill out the <a href="/suggest/">Suggest a brand</a> form. Listings are free, and anyone can suggest a brand, including the brand itself. It helps to tell us where you're based, when you were founded, and which parts of your products, if any, are made in America. We check every suggestion before adding it.
      - id: corrections
        q: "Can I suggest changes to an existing listing?"
        a: >-
          Yes, please. Use the <a href="/update/">Update a listing</a> form, or the "Update this listing" link at the bottom of any brand page, which fills in the brand for you. A link to a source helps us check the change quickly.
      - id: removed
        q: "Why was a brand removed or marked inactive?"
        a: >-
          We mark a company "No longer trading" or "Defunct" when its website and social accounts have gone quiet or it has announced it has closed. We keep these listings because they're part of the history. We remove a listing when we can't confirm the company exists or where it's based, or when it turns out to be based outside North America. If we got it wrong, <a href="/update/">let us know</a>.
      - id: forms
        q: "What happens when I send a form?"
        a: >-
          It comes straight to our inbox. We read everything, and we usually reply or update the listing within a week. We're volunteers, so it can sometimes take longer.
      - id: advertising
        q: "Can I advertise or sponsor a listing?"
        a: >-
          No. The directory is non-commercial, with no ads or sponsored listings. If you'd like to support it or collaborate, <a href="/contact.html">get in touch</a>.
  - title: "Our information"
    items:
      - id: sources
        q: "Where does your information come from, and how do you check it?"
        a: >-
          From companies' own websites and social accounts, information brands send us, and watch publications. Brand pages list the sources we used where we have them. When sources disagree, for example on a founding year, we leave the detail out rather than guess. Brands can confirm or correct their own details through the update form.
      - id: updates
        q: "How often is the directory updated?"
        a: >-
          Whenever we add companies or get corrections, which is usually several times a month. Each brand page shows when it was last updated, and the homepage shows recently added brands.
      - id: data
        q: "Can I use your data or logos?"
        a: >-
          The directory data is free to download as a <a href="/american-watch-makers.csv">spreadsheet (CSV)</a> or <a href="/brands.json">JSON</a>. You're welcome to reuse it with a credit and link back to the American Watchmaking Directory. Logos and trademarks belong to their brands, so please ask the brand before using them.
  - title: "About us"
    items:
      - id: who-runs-it
        q: "Who runs the directory?"
        a: >-
          Two watch enthusiasts in Seattle, Washington: Hamza (Head of Partnerships at WatchCharts and an organizer of the Seattle RedBar chapter) and Vivek (Software Development Engineer at Expedia). It's a side project; neither of us is paid for it.
      - id: affiliation
        q: "Are you affiliated with any of the listed brands?"
        a: >-
          No. We aren't paid by or affiliated with any brand in the directory, listings are free, and there are no paid placements. Hamza's job at WatchCharts doesn't influence who is listed or what we write; WatchCharts has no role in the directory.
      - id: personal-data
        q: "Do you collect any personal data?"
        a: >-
          We use Google Analytics, which sets cookies, to see how many people visit and which pages they use. Forms are handled by Formspree, a form service that sends your message to our email, and the maps load map tiles from OpenFreeMap. We don't sell your information or show ads. The <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> has the details, including how to opt out of analytics.
      - id: whats-next
        q: "Will you add more brands or features?"
        a: >-
          Yes. We add companies as we find them or as people suggest them, and we welcome ideas for the site through the <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>.
---
{% extends "prose.njk" %}

{% block head %}
    <script type="application/ld+json">{{ {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": groups | faqSchema
    } | json | safe }}</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
                {% for g in groups %}
                <h2>{{ g.title }}</h2>
                <div class="faq-group">
                    {% for item in g.items %}
                    <details class="faq" id="{{ item.id }}">
                        <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
                        <div class="faq-a"><p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p></div>
                    </details>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
